# Grants non-root users (group "plugdev", which a normal desktop user
# account is a member of on Debian/Ubuntu by default) read/write access to
# RTL2832U-based SDR dongles - without this, opening the device as a plain
# user fails with a permission error, and since this app's "auto" driver
# mode silently falls back to the Simulated backend on ANY open failure
# (by design - see AGENTS.md gotcha 8, so a genuinely missing/unplugged
# device doesn't wedge the scanner), that permission failure looks
# identical to "no hardware detected" from the user's side - a real,
# reported case on a fresh Ubuntu VM with no other RTL-SDR software
# ever installed to provide this rule already (e.g. the `rtl-sdr` apt
# package ships an equivalent rule, but this self-contained .deb
# deliberately doesn't depend on it - see packaging/linux-deb/README.md).
#
# 0bda:2832 / 0bda:2838 are the two RTL2832U-based Vendor:Product IDs the
# overwhelming majority of real RTL-SDR dongles (including RTL-SDR Blog
# V3/V4) report as - covers what this project's own hardware was tested
# against. A different SDR (HackRF, LimeSDR, ...) needs SoapySDR anyway
# (not supported by this build - see README.md), so isn't covered here.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0bda", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2832", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0666"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0bda", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2838", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0666"
